# WeiDU install console tabs

Install console has three tabs. Do not mix their roles.

## Do

- **WeiDU tab** — raw WeiDU process stdout/stderr only (`InstallEventPayload::Output` / `run-stdout.log` + `run-stderr.log`).
- **Commands tab** — setup command lines (`CommandLogged`) and all **app-synthesized** status / info / error text (`Classified`, `pushConsoleLine`, pause/stop/snapshot messages); mirrored to `run-commands.log`.
- **Results tab** — keyword highlights via `consoleLineTone` from WeiDU output (and app lines only when they intentionally go through that helper); mirrored to `run-results.log`.
- UI keeps / reloads only a capped tail of each tab (~800 lines); full history stays on disk.
- On **project open** (Install station may still be hidden), load all three tab tails from the run log files once per `runId`/`logDir`.

## Don't

- Do **not** append app `Classified` / status / `[info]` / `[error]` lines to the WeiDU (`consoleLines`) stream.
- Do **not** re-emit stream-classified error/warning phrases as `Classified` into the UI — raw `Output` already feeds WeiDU + Results.
- Do **not** invent a fourth console channel without an explicit request.
- Do **not** grow unbounded React console arrays — always `trimConsoleLines` (same cap for WeiDU, Commands, and Results).
- Do **not** store console line arrays in localStorage; disk logs + `run-state.json` are the source of truth.

